=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
After exhaustive inspection of every BGP session, routing table, interface state, and FRR log in the dc_clos_bgp fabric, no fault was found. End-to-end connectivity between pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) and pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) is fully operational: a live ping confirms 4/4 packets received with zero loss, and a traceroute traces the complete four-hop path pc_0_0 → leaf_router_0_0 → spine_router_0_0 → leaf_router_0_1 → pc_0_1. All seven eBGP sessions across the CLOS fabric (leaf↔spine, spine↔super_spine) are in the Established state with zero drops. Every router holds a correct FIB: both leaf routers know each other's /24 host subnet, both spines carry full leaf reachability, and the super_spine holds dual-path BGP entries for both prefixes. All physical interfaces are UP/LOWER_UP with no errors. The one apparent anomaly — spine_router_0_0 receiving 0 prefixes from super_spine_router_0 — is normal BGP behaviour: the super_spine re-advertises both leaf prefixes with AS 65100 still in their AS_PATH, so spine_router_0_0 correctly discards them to prevent routing loops. The startup "nexthop_set failed" messages in the FRR logs are a benign race condition during container boot and resolve within one second. The user's report of unreachability is a false premise: the network was either self-healed before the investigation began or the complaint was inaccurate. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===